<title>SWITZERLAND: GM EUROPE FINANCE HEAD DIES OF HEART ATTACK.</title>
<headline>GM EUROPE FINANCE HEAD DIES OF HEART ATTACK.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carmaker General Motors Corp said on Tuesday Gail Gunderson, vice president for finance at GM Europe, had died of a heart attack aged 60.</p>
<p>Gunderson took over the financial post at Zurich-based GM Europe, which runs GM's global operations outside North America, in September 1996.</p>
<p>Gunderson joined GM in 1964 and spent most of his career in Europe, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>He had been director of finance at British unit Vauxhall Motors Ltd  from 1986 through 1991, and then board member in charge of finance at Germany's Adam Opel AG before moving to Zurich.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
